1
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:12,060
Who is he? Where?

2
00:00:13,350 --> 00:00:15,180
Which one? That guy?

3
00:00:17,010 --> 00:00:22,810
For Lost Love

4
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:20,550
Oh, him? The one lying
facedown on the table?

5
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:23,970
That's right. That youngster.

6
00:00:23,970 --> 00:00:26,230
Okay, okay. I see.

7
00:00:26,230 --> 00:00:28,830
He looks like someone who'd do that.

8
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:32,000
He's the guy who lost to a pig.

9
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:35,870
Guys like him really do exist.

10
00:00:35,870 --> 00:00:40,280
I'm amazed he had the balls to say
he wanted to join the king's guard.

11
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:43,790
So, what did you want?

12
00:00:43,790 --> 00:00:47,410
All we have to do is
tell him he's been rejected?

13
00:00:47,410 --> 00:00:50,050
That's right. All you need to do
is convey the message.

14
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:53,420
Fine, I guess.

15
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:55,430
Aw, damn.

16
00:00:56,030 --> 00:00:59,190
I'm not sure I can keep myself
from doing more.

17
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,810
You want to mock him?

18
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:04,800
I mean, just look at his stupid face.

19
00:01:08,230 --> 00:01:11,850
Go on. I'll buy you drinks later.

20
00:01:11,850 --> 00:01:13,150
Okay.

21
00:01:13,710 --> 00:01:15,220
Quit laughing so much.

22
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:16,740
Yeah, but...

23
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:37,980
You lot look just as stupid as he does.

24
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:18,560
Olmar?

25
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:23,870
Olmar, do you have a minute?

26
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,570
My name is Brodd.

27
00:03:31,570 --> 00:03:33,830
I'm a member of the king's guard.

28
00:03:36,230 --> 00:03:37,420
And?

29
00:03:37,810 --> 00:03:43,430
I've brought a message from Wulf,
captain of His Majesty's guard.

30
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:45,580
You're here to tell me I've been rejected.

31
00:03:46,390 --> 00:03:49,610
Now, now. I'm here on a job.

32
00:03:49,610 --> 00:03:51,920
Allow me to deliver my message.

33
00:03:55,990 --> 00:04:02,380
Olmar, regarding your request
to join the king's guard,

34
00:04:02,770 --> 00:04:05,790
the captain spoke highly
of your determination

35
00:04:05,790 --> 00:04:09,830
to offer your life in service of His Majesty.

36
00:04:11,390 --> 00:04:16,590
However, upon seeing your skill with a sword,

37
00:04:17,390 --> 00:04:20,580
he remarked that your skills
"need improvement."

38
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:27,960
Therefore, we regret to inform you that...

39
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:32,510
Regret to inform you that...

40
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:46,870
Th-There's nothing regrettable about it.
You lost to a pig!

41
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:51,650
Don't say that.

42
00:04:51,650 --> 00:04:53,280
I-I can't breathe.

43
00:04:54,750 --> 00:04:58,940
I heard... I heard you
couldn't even cut a pig.

44
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:04,130
Why not? Was the pig wearing
chain mail? A hauberk perhaps?

45
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:07,920
Oh, but on a pig,
I guess you'd call it a hogberk.

46
00:05:16,910 --> 00:05:20,650
Forgive me. I shouldn't laugh.

47
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:24,360
He failed to get a job.

48
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:28,030
Do you guys know anyone who's hiring?

49
00:05:28,630 --> 00:05:32,660
Come to think of it,
the castle was looking for a new cook.

50
00:05:33,010 --> 00:05:36,300
That won't work. He can't chop up pigs!

51
00:05:45,930 --> 00:05:47,180
I'm dying!

52
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:05,070
A warrior answers insults with his sword!

53
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:06,760
Draw your weapon!

54
00:06:13,730 --> 00:06:16,050
But you couldn't even cut a pig.

55
00:06:16,650 --> 00:06:19,550
I'm dying! I'm gonna die laughing!

56
00:06:22,130 --> 00:06:22,630
Whoa!

57
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,120
What's your problem?

58
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:29,400
You'll hurt someone doing that, you weakling.

59
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:36,510
Come on, let's go.

60
00:06:36,510 --> 00:06:37,300
Wait for me.

61
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:38,390
It's a fight!

62
00:06:38,390 --> 00:06:40,650
There's a five-on-one
happening by the stalls!

63
00:06:40,950 --> 00:06:42,540
They've got swords!

64
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:45,070
Someone's gonna bleed!

65
00:06:46,050 --> 00:06:46,810
Get him!

66
00:06:46,810 --> 00:06:48,160
Kill him!

67
00:06:48,430 --> 00:06:50,340
You've got this, young one!

68
00:06:50,340 --> 00:06:52,050
I'll take him on myself.

69
00:06:52,050 --> 00:06:56,660
We'd dishonor ourselves as warriors if we
ganged up on a guy who can't even cut a pig.

70
00:06:57,710 --> 00:06:58,960
You'd better not lose.

71
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:03,860
Look at you, all excited to fight.

72
00:07:05,050 --> 00:07:08,750
I'll help you train, Olmar.

73
00:07:15,660 --> 00:07:18,060
Come on, stand up. You can do it.

74
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:30,600
He's as pathetic as I was told.

75
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:53,480
Stand up, Olmar.

76
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:56,560
Don't lie on the ground during a duel.

77
00:08:03,070 --> 00:08:04,160
Thorgil...

78
00:08:06,070 --> 00:08:10,840
Thorgil, they... they humiliated me.

79
00:08:11,830 --> 00:08:13,420
I know. I can see that.

80
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:16,540
Get back on your feet and kill him.

81
00:08:26,550 --> 00:08:27,480
Stand up.

82
00:08:35,740 --> 00:08:37,940
Stand up, Olmar!

83
00:08:45,750 --> 00:08:48,660
Th-Thorgil, I...

84
00:08:49,390 --> 00:08:50,980
Listen to me, Olmar.

85
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:54,870
There are only two options for a
warrior who has been insulted.

86
00:08:55,580 --> 00:08:57,560
Kill or die.

87
00:08:58,100 --> 00:09:00,000
If you can't kill him, then you'll die here.

88
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:07,860
I won't allow you to go on living
without addressing this insult.

89
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:11,540
Fight and become a man.

90
00:09:12,110 --> 00:09:14,430
Today is the day.

91
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:16,890
Thor...

92
00:09:16,890 --> 00:09:17,910
Go on.

93
00:09:21,990 --> 00:09:23,390
What the hell was that?

94
00:09:24,870 --> 00:09:26,950
Imagine it, Olmar.

95
00:09:26,950 --> 00:09:29,780
Imagine the moment you
cut off your enemy's head.

96
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:31,780
Y-Yeah...

97
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:35,080
Let me hear you. Say it from your stomach.

98
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:36,780
Yeah.

99
00:09:36,780 --> 00:09:37,750
Louder.

100
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:38,780
Yeah!

101
00:09:39,430 --> 00:09:40,890
Imagine it.

102
00:09:40,890 --> 00:09:45,040
Imagine your enemy crying with remorse in a
pool of blood with his guts strewn about him.

103
00:09:45,370 --> 00:09:46,670
Yeah!

104
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:49,170
Show some spirit, Olmar!

105
00:09:49,170 --> 00:09:50,380
Yeah!

106
00:09:50,380 --> 00:09:53,050
Kill the bastard! Kill him!

107
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:53,990
Yeah!

108
00:09:53,990 --> 00:09:56,030
Go!

109
00:09:59,690 --> 00:10:03,640
Uh-oh. Provoke him, and all of
a sudden, he's raring to go.

110
00:10:08,070 --> 00:10:10,720
The time for practice is over.

111
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:49,780
Seriously?

112
00:10:51,110 --> 00:10:51,870
Hey!

113
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:53,730
You bastard!

114
00:10:54,220 --> 00:10:55,850
Don't let him escape alive.

115
00:10:55,850 --> 00:10:58,470
We'll reclaim our honor here and now.

116
00:10:58,470 --> 00:10:59,370
Yeah.

117
00:11:00,790 --> 00:11:04,740
Well done, Olmar. That's my little brother.

118
00:11:07,870 --> 00:11:09,590
Leave the rest to me.

119
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:28,390
He's dead...

120
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:32,360
Did I kill him?

121
00:11:53,790 --> 00:11:56,980
I killed a man...

122
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:17,300
So it was his eye.

123
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:21,150
It was damaged by a rock or something.

124
00:12:23,430 --> 00:12:25,410
Olmar! Thorgil!

125
00:12:25,950 --> 00:12:28,300
Move. Get out of the way.

126
00:12:33,710 --> 00:12:37,360
Wh-Wh-What is this?

127
00:12:38,420 --> 00:12:39,760
What happened?

128
00:12:43,350 --> 00:12:44,550
Y-You...

129
00:12:50,470 --> 00:12:52,440
Calm down, Dad.

130
00:12:53,070 --> 00:12:55,690
Calm down? You want me to calm down?

131
00:12:55,950 --> 00:12:59,800
You... You killed the king's men!

132
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:03,410
What are you going to do about this?

133
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:05,660
We did nothing wrong.

134
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:06,980
What?

135
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:09,620
Olmar was insulted, so he fought a duel.

136
00:13:09,620 --> 00:13:10,990
He defended his honor.

137
00:13:10,990 --> 00:13:11,910
But...

138
00:13:12,210 --> 00:13:13,670
There were five of them.

139
00:13:13,670 --> 00:13:17,250
No one could object to me joining the fight.

140
00:13:17,820 --> 00:13:20,480
You're his father.
You should be praising him.

141
00:13:24,540 --> 00:13:27,640
Duels are forbidden by law!

142
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:31,520
Nobody cares about that law.

143
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:38,400
They had swords. They must've known
insulting him would be costly.

144
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:41,630
They knew that, and insulted him regardless.

145
00:13:41,630 --> 00:13:44,400
The churls deserved to die.

146
00:13:47,930 --> 00:13:50,240
Move. Clear the way.

147
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:50,910
Hey, what's going on?

148
00:13:51,650 --> 00:13:53,470
It's... It's the guards.

149
00:13:53,470 --> 00:13:57,020
We did nothing wrong.
Duels happen all the time.

150
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:59,140
Normally we wouldn't be punished.

151
00:14:03,510 --> 00:14:09,120
Who dared to start a commotion
just outside His Majesty's castle?

152
00:14:10,620 --> 00:14:13,480
Step forward and present yourselves.

153
00:14:16,060 --> 00:14:19,310
What's going on here? Olmar is alive.

154
00:14:19,820 --> 00:14:23,130
Ketil's here, too. Who's the other one?

155
00:14:23,130 --> 00:14:26,960
I don't know. Probably a family member.

156
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:32,940
I am Thorgil, son of Ketil,
member of the king's guard.

157
00:14:33,370 --> 00:14:36,310
This is my father, Ketil,
and my younger brother, Olmar.

158
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:38,830
This was a fair duel.

159
00:14:39,560 --> 00:14:41,390
We have done nothing wrong.

160
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:46,590
Silence. The king has forbidden duels.

161
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:54,280
You've disrespected the king.
You're all under arrest.

162
00:14:55,130 --> 00:14:56,940
I-I knew it.

163
00:14:56,940 --> 00:14:59,760
See? I told you so, Thorgil!

164
00:15:05,260 --> 00:15:06,900
Come on, hands behind your back.

165
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:07,950
Stop resisting.

166
00:15:08,330 --> 00:15:10,910
W-W-Wait a minute. I didn't—

167
00:15:12,190 --> 00:15:14,840
Hand over your sword and
put your hands behind your back.

168
00:15:17,180 --> 00:15:18,830
Hey, are you deaf?

169
00:15:31,260 --> 00:15:32,400
What?

170
00:15:33,950 --> 00:15:36,020
You... You asshole!

171
00:16:08,510 --> 00:16:10,010
Bastard!

172
00:16:24,190 --> 00:16:27,400
H-Have you actually lost
your mind this time, Thorgil?

173
00:16:27,780 --> 00:16:30,900
It's over. There's no coming back from this.

174
00:16:34,550 --> 00:16:37,910
There's something I want to ask you.

175
00:16:39,870 --> 00:16:43,940
I'm not a patient man.
Be careful how you answer my question.

176
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:46,160
If you tell me, I'll spare your life.

177
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:50,390
Why did you allow Olmar to win?

178
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:52,230
What?

179
00:16:52,940 --> 00:16:55,110
They... let me win?

180
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:57,080
Tell me.

181
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:58,560
I-I don't know—

182
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:08,780
You should heed people's warnings.

183
00:17:09,910 --> 00:17:13,360
Tell me. Why did you set up Olmar?

184
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:22,380
To... To arrest Ketil.

185
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:31,300
We had Olmar kill the king's men
so Ketil would be held responsible

186
00:17:32,110 --> 00:17:35,100
for his son's disrespect to the king.

187
00:17:38,540 --> 00:17:42,620
Wh-What did I do to deserve that?

188
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:48,520
I-I simply followed Captain Wulf's orders.

189
00:17:49,320 --> 00:17:51,900
Please, let me tend to my wounds.

190
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:56,110
The blood... It won't stop!

191
00:17:57,760 --> 00:18:01,420
It's over. King Canute
has set his sights on us.

192
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:07,190
No, Dad.

193
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:10,670
Thorgil...

194
00:18:12,060 --> 00:18:14,420
This is the beginning.

195
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:17,080
Our enemy is strong.

196
00:18:38,900 --> 00:18:43,030
I see. So Ketil's family escaped.

197
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:46,460
I'm sorry, Your Majesty.

198
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:51,270
I sent men to secure their ships and
lodgings, but they haven't been found.

199
00:18:51,980 --> 00:18:53,710
We're currently searching for them.

200
00:18:54,380 --> 00:18:58,600
It's my fault that we failed to capture Thorgil.

201
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:02,850
He sounds like a skilled warrior.

202
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:05,620
Yes. He was a good subordinate.

203
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,200
It doesn't affect our plans.

204
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:12,180
We have our excuse to punish them.

205
00:19:12,810 --> 00:19:15,730
As planned, we'll head to Ketil's farm.

206
00:19:16,710 --> 00:19:19,200
If Ketil isn't there, then that's fine.

207
00:19:19,620 --> 00:19:23,450
If he is and resists us,
then we'll simply overwhelm him.

208
00:19:23,450 --> 00:19:28,400
Yes, Your Majesty.
I'll mobilize 32 of your guard.

209
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:34,630
With 70 of Floki's Jomsvikings,
we'll have 102 men altogether.

210
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:39,020
That should be enough.
When will Floki arrive?

211
00:19:39,670 --> 00:19:42,230
Within three days, from Jomsborg.

212
00:19:44,180 --> 00:19:47,560
Then we'll leave at dawn three days from now.

213
00:19:48,350 --> 00:19:49,110
Leave me.

214
00:19:49,850 --> 00:19:50,600
Yes, Your Majesty.

215
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,910
What are you laughing about, King Sweyn?

216
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:22,390
Don't be so angry.

217
00:20:22,810 --> 00:20:30,280
Why shouldn't a father be pleased
his son is beginning to resemble himself?

218
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:39,400
Keep going.

219
00:20:40,750 --> 00:20:48,340
You'll need to pile up plenty of
bodies to reach the top.

220
00:21:03,910 --> 00:21:09,190
All right, gentlemen. You can come out now.

221
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:17,190
These barrels reek of salt.

222
00:21:19,120 --> 00:21:23,750
You saved us, Leif.
I appreciate your kindness.

223
00:21:24,350 --> 00:21:26,860
This isn't an act of kindness. It's a deal.

224
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:29,950
Don't forget the promise you made me.

225
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:35,960
I wouldn't smuggle criminals
out of mere kindness.

226
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:33,260
Boy, that stinks.

227
00:21:36,290 --> 00:21:40,600
Do you have any idea how difficult
it was to convince my men?

228
00:21:41,830 --> 00:21:45,260
Don't worry. A warrior
never goes back on his word.

229
00:21:45,830 --> 00:21:51,390
Ketil's farm will buy all your
cargo for triple its value.

230
00:21:52,350 --> 00:21:54,440
Don't forget about Thorfinn, too.

231
00:21:54,790 --> 00:21:58,230
Of course. You can have the slave, too.

232
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:00,570
Right, Dad?

233
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:06,950
Dad, you can come out now.

234
00:22:06,950 --> 00:22:08,850
Shut up!

235
00:22:08,850 --> 00:22:12,450
Don't talk to me. Leave me alone.

236
00:22:13,120 --> 00:22:15,040
He's in a bad mood.

237
00:22:15,790 --> 00:22:18,870
Don't forget our promise.

238
00:22:51,040 --> 00:22:54,190
All right. That's enough for today.

239
00:22:54,740 --> 00:22:56,900
Yeah.

240
00:22:56,900 --> 00:22:58,320
Good work today.

241
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:15,020
What's the matter, Thorfinn?

242
00:23:15,790 --> 00:23:18,060
Is the sunset that captivating?

243
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:22,870
No...

244
00:23:29,380 --> 00:23:31,680
Mock me if you wish.

245
00:23:32,980 --> 00:23:35,270
Curse me if you must.

246
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:41,000
I do all of this to create my utopia.

247
00:23:45,990 --> 00:23:50,500
All for lost love.

248
00:25:36,700 --> 00:25:40,080
Dark Clouds

249
00:25:38,020 --> 00:25:39,230
"Dark Clouds."
